Current logic of cron job is:

* fetch xx records (as defined in the limit) per system_type
* limit the fetched records by limit defined in the above config _(this seems not ok at the moment as we have multiple pending tokens but will be ok once we match the token creation vs deletion on daily basis)_
* process the records one by one
* cron is processing records in parallel (2 records at once)
* with this load, cron is taking 4-6 minutes to process 5000 tokens (one by one)

Based on above config, the cron job will be manage to process (delete) roughly 720000 tokens per day (5000 x 10 minutes = 30000 token in 1 hour,  30000 x 24 hr = 720000)

