Thank you for the interesting case.

*Please find answers to your questions below:*

{{is it okay to ask referrer to provide some details about referee? }}

It’s ok since the referrer is responsible for ensuring that they provide this data legally and the referee is informed that their data is shared with Bolt. 
However, we have an obligation to inform the referee on how Bolt processes this shared data: name, email, etc. 

*Solution:*
If you have a platform when the referrer shares these details, we can put a wording there that

i) referrer is personally responsible that the referee has been informed about their data being shared with Bolt for this purpose, 

ii) put a privacy policy on how we process referee personal data for this program asking the referrer to send this policy to the referee, 

iii) control that before we contact or process referee’s personal data for this program, we have informed the referee about the processing by Bolt.

{color:#bf2600}Could you please send a link to the platform/solution we use for referring couriers?{color}


{{what exactly we can share with those 'old couriers'?}}
Currently we give this 'old courier' an update:

* If new courier did not finish registration -{{ we say that registration was not completed}} -{color:#bf2600} what is the purpose we share this with the referrer? if this information is not related to any payments due to old courier, etc, we should definitely exclude it since we may not be able to find a legal basis for sharing these details.{color}
* If new courier joined after campaign has ended - {{we say that as well}} - {color:#bf2600}what is the purpose we share this with the referrer? if this information is not related to any payments due to old courier, etc, we should definitely exclude it since we may not be able to find a legal basis for sharing these details.{color}
* If all campaign conditions are met - {{we advise referrer when bonus will be paid out.}} -{color:#bf2600} I recommend only informing when the bonus will be paid off without disclosing that new courier didn’t met the campaign provisions. If we state to the referrer that the campaign provisions haven’t been met because of referrer’s wrong actions, we can disclose it. But I recommend excluding the provision of information about the new courier to the old courier.{color}

