I have investigated this issue and here are my findings:
In {{FetchInitialAppStateSuspendingInteractor}}'s {{handleSuccess}} function, we have this logic below

{noformat}if (authInfo != null) {
    saveAuthorizationInteractor.execute(authInfo)
} else {
    processAuthErrorInteractor.execute(
        ProcessAuthErrorInteractor.Args(
            error = LoggedOutException("No user identified on startup"),
            clearAuthenticator = false
        )
    )
}{noformat}

when updating from 77 to 78, there is no {{login_state}} property in the {{appState/get/v1}}  response, this property is parsed to the {{authInfo}} field in the app when it is {{null}} and we receive {{null}} {{authInfo}}. Thus {{processAuthErrorInteractor}} is executed where we do

{noformat}override fun execute(args: Args) {
        if (args.error !is LoggedOutException) {
            logger.e(args.error, "Non-fatal error occurred in login repository")
        }
        val userEvent = UserEvent(null, args.error)
        if (userEvent.isTaxifyError() || userEvent.error is LoggedOutException) {
            savedUserRepository.cleanImmediately("ProcessAuthErrorInteractor execute")
            if (args.clearAuthenticator) {
                authenticator.cleanImmediately()
            }
        }
        userEventRepository.publishUserEvent(userEvent)
    }{noformat}

And I believe that might be the reason why we experience logout when updating the app from 77 to 78. I could not find out why we do not I do not have the {{login_state}} in the {{appState/get/v1}} response when updating from 77 to 78. Before 78 we do not have this problem, for example, updating from 76.1 to 77 is fine. I think we need BE support to investigate further.

